-- Plan 55 criterion 7's witness: a discarded `Result` is reported against the
-- `.sdx`, and it is rustc's warning carried back rather than a Redox lint.
--
-- The criterion asked for *"a Redox lint, not only a rustc warning"*, and leaf
-- 4 worded the value as position — *"the discard lints at the Redox line
-- rather than rustc's"*. The position is already here, which is what this
-- fixture records: plan 07's remapping puts `unused_must_use` on the author's
-- own line and column, the generated file is never named, and the build still
-- succeeds because a discard is legal.
--
-- No `RDX1004` was added, and the two statements below are why.
--
-- `save 1` is the **only** shape a lexical lint could see: `save`'s return
-- type is written in this file, so "a call to a Result-returning function,
-- discarded" is decidable from the source with no types — doc 03 §2's
-- admission test. `u8::try_from 300` is the shape that actually bites, and
-- nothing in this file says it returns anything at all. Knowing that needs
-- the standard library's signatures, which is the type checker AGENTS.md
-- forbids Redox growing.
--
-- So a Redox lint would fire only where rustc already fires, and stay silent
-- on the case the criterion exists for — a lint whose coverage is a strict
-- subset of the warning it was meant to improve on. Plan 56 leaf 3 and plan
-- 59 criterion 5 were both withdrawn on that reasoning; this is the third.
--
-- And the suppression story is already complete: `#[allow(unused_must_use)]`
-- on the line above silences it, because the emitter passes an attribute that
-- is not Redox's own straight through. Measured 2026-11-10.
save : i32 -> Result<i32, String>
save n = Ok n

main : ()
main =
  save 1
  u8::try_from 300
  print "done"
  ()
